WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.111 --> 00:00:00.953
(audience cheering)
- Say hi to Taylor.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.353
- The winner.

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:04.186
The winner.
- I know.

00:00:04.186 --> 00:00:05.019
- The winner. The winner.
- The winner. The winner.

00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:06.180
- Of "American Idol" is-
- The winner.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.190
- He's literally only said
that to so many people.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.023
We're two of 'em.

00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:10.066
That's so cool.
(Ryan laughing)

00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:11.070
- Great to see you guys.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.040
- I found out something
new that I did not know.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.600
I didn't know that you were originally...

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.400
They maybe almost had you as a judge?

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.730
- Yeah, originally when the
producers, Nigel and Ken-

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.340
- Yeah.
- Were setting up the show,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.650
they had heard me on the
radio here in Los Angeles

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.230
and they thought that
I might fit the panel

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.260
to be up there with whoever
else was already on.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.093
- Yeah.
- I guess Simon

00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:32.926
was already on board

00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:33.759
and I don't know who else at that point.

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:35.730
And I was like, "Well wait a minute.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.890
I would love to audition to be the host."

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.490
And so I auditioned
eventually to be the host-

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.220
- Yeah.
- And I got the job.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.600
So I'm happy to still have the job.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.680
- I know, that's incredible.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.910
I just, I was like,
(audience cheering)

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.310
what would it be like if you initially

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.660
were one of the judges?
- See, the problem is

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.820
I'm like in auto host mode all the time

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.220
so I don't know that I'd be
able to sit behind the desk

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.210
and just give feedback.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.890
I'd want to do that,
then toss to commercial.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.102
Welcome back. How are you?

00:00:57.102 --> 00:00:58.470
(Kelly laughing)
You know, all the...

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.700
And that would be too much.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.486
- Are you like this in life?

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:02.710
Like when you're with family-
- Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.010
- Or like on a date, you're
just like, "Wait, I'm sorry,

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:05.843
I'm trying not to-"
- On a date,

00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:08.010
"Good evening. How are you?"
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.860
- We would like to have
the nachos followed by...

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.133
I think, would you like the fajitas?

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:12.966
- I just mean-
- Matter of fact,

00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:14.010
let's have the beef and chicken fajitas

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.672
and we'll be right back
after we use the bathroom.

00:01:15.672 --> 00:01:16.505
(Kelly and audience laughing)

